:PT.:PK.*CCSID:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID determines the conversion.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSMTPA/TBLSMTPIN'.Incoming ASCII/EBCDIC table (TBLSMTPIN)
:P.The incoming ASCII/EBCDIC table for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*CCSID:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID determines the conversion.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSMTPA/FIREWALL'.Firewall (FIREWALL)
:P.The firewall for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSMTPA/ALLMAILMSF'.Journal all mail on MSF (ALLMAILMSF)
:P.The journal all mail on MSF for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSMTPA/DIALSCD'.Dial-up scheduler (DIALSCD)
:P.The dial-up scheduler for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Scheduler
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Connection profile
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Timer
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 1440.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSMTPA/ETRNCLT'.Support ETRN for client (ETRNCLT)
:P.The support ETRN for client for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Client
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Domain name
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 40 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Server
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSMTPA/ALWIMPSSL'.Allow e-mail over implicit SSL (ALWIMPSSL)
:P.The allow e-mail over implicit SSL for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSMTPA/MAXINEMM'.Max incoming e-mail messages (MAXINEMM)
:P.The max incoming e-mail messages for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 1240000.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSMTPA/MAXOUTEMM'.Max outgoing e-mail messages (MAXOUTEMM)
:P.The max outgoing e-mail messages for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 1240000.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSMTPA/KEEPUNTIL'.Keep e-mail until (KEEPUNTIL)
:P.The keep e-mail until for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Incoming
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 1240000.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Outgoing
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 1240000.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSMTPA/MAXEMMSIZE'.Maximum e-mail size (MAXEMMSIZE)
:P.The maximum e-mail size for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1000 to 2000000.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSMTPA/ALIASDMN'.Alias domain (ALIASDMN)
:P.The alias domain for this command.
:P.Up to 10 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 385 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSMTPA/OAUTH'.OAuth (OAUTH)
:P.The OAuth for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Client ID
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 255 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Action
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DELETE:EPK.
:PD.Deleted.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ENABLE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=STRTCPFTP.Start TCP/IP File Transfer (FTP)
:P.The Start TCP/IP File Transfer (FTP) command works with the FTP
client.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRTCPFTP/RMTSYS'.Remote system (RMTSYS)
:P.The remote system, by host name or internet address.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*INTNETADR:EPK.
:PD.The internet address given in INTNETADR.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 255 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRTCPFTP/INTNETADR'.Internet address (INTNETADR)
:P.An internet address in dotted decimal form (IPv4) or in colon form
(IPv6).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 64 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRTCPFTP/CCSID'.Coded character set identifier (CCSID)
:P.The coded character set identifier&colon. the code page and character
set the data is in, or is to be converted to.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65533.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRTCPFTP/TBLFTPOUT'.Outgoing EBCDIC/ASCII table (TBLFTPOUT)
:P.The outgoing EBCDIC/ASCII table for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CCSID:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID determines the conversion.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRTCPFTP/TBLFTPIN'.Incoming ASCII/EBCDIC table (TBLFTPIN)
:P.The incoming ASCII/EBCDIC table for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CCSID:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID determines the conversion.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRTCPFTP/PORT'.Port (PORT)
:P.The TCP or UDP port number.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SECURE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRTCPFTP/SECCNN'.Secure connection (SECCNN)
:P.Whether the connection is secured with TLS.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*KERBEROS:EPK.
:PD.Kerberos.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SSL, *IMPLICIT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRTCPFTP/DTAPROT'.Data protection (DTAPROT)
:P.The data protection for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PK.*PRIVATE:EPK.
:PD.Private authorities.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CLEAR, *SAFE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRTCPFTP/APPID'.Application identifier (APPID)
:P.The application identifier.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 100 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=LPR.Send TCP/IP Spooled File (LPR)
:P.Use the Send TCP/IP Spooled File (LPR) command to send a spooled file
to a remote system's line printer daemon; the same command as
SNDTCPSPLF, under its other name.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='LPR/RMTSYS'.Remote system (RMTSYS)
:P.The remote system, by host name or internet address.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*INTNETADR:EPK.
:PD.The internet address given in INTNETADR.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 255 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='LPR/PRTQ'.Printer queue (PRTQ)
:P.The printer queue for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 255 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='LPR/FILE'.Spooled file (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='LPR/JOB'.Job name (JOB)
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:PARML.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.User&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Number&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters. The value must be from 000000 to 999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='LPR/SPLNBR'.Spooled file number (SPLNBR)
:P.The number of the spooled file among the job's spooled files of the
same name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:PT.:PK.*ANY:EPK.
:PD.Any value matches.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='LPR/JOBSYSNAME'.Job system name (JOBSYSNAME)
:P.The name of the system the job ran on, which tells apart spooled
files that came from other systems.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PK.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PK.*ANY:EPK.
:PD.Any value matches.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='LPR/CRTDATE'.Spooled file created (CRTDATE)
:P.The date and time the spooled file was created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Creation date
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Creation time
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:PT.:PV.time:EPV.
:PD.Type a time of day&colon. hours, minutes and seconds.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='LPR/DESTTYP'.Destination type (DESTTYP)
:P.The destination type for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*AS400:EPK.
:PD.This system's native format.
:PT.:PK DEF.*OTHER:EPK.
:PD.Other.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PSF2.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='LPR/TRANSFORM'.Transform SCS to ASCII (TRANSFORM)
:P.Whether the host print transform converts the SCS data to the
printer's ASCII data stream.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='LPR/USRDTATFM'.User data transform (USRDTATFM)
:P.The program that transforms the user data of a spooled file before it
is sent to the printer.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='LPR/MFRTYPMDL'.Manufacturer type and model (MFRTYPMDL)
:P.The manufacturer type and model for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 15 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, *IBM42011 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='LPR/INTNETADR'.Internet address (INTNETADR)
:P.An internet address in dotted decimal form (IPv4) or in colon form
(IPv6).
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 15 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='LPR/WSCST'.Workstation customizing object (WSCST)
:P.The workstation customizing object that describes the printer to the
host print transform.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='LPR/DLTSPLF'.Delete file after sending (DLTSPLF)
:P.Whether to delete file after sending.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='LPR/DESTOPT'.Destination-dependent options (DESTOPT)
:P.Options passed to the remote system that receives the spooled file.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 128 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='LPR/SEPPAGE'.Print separator page (SEPPAGE)
:P.Whether a separator page prints before each spooled file.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=SNDSMTPEMM.Send SMTP E-mail Message (SNDSMTPEMM)
:P.Use the Send SMTP E-mail Message (SNDSMTPEMM) command to send an
e-mail through the mail router CHGSMTPA names (net/mail).
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDSMTPEMM/RCP'.Recipient (RCP)
:P.The recipient for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Recipient address
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Recipient type
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PRI, *CC, *BCC.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDSMTPEMM/SUBJECT'.Subject (SUBJECT)
:P.The subject for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDSMTPEMM/NOTE'.Note (NOTE)
:P.The note for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDSMTPEMM/ATTACH'.Attachment (ATTACH)
:P.The attachment for this command.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Attachment name
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Content type
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OCTET, *PLAIN, *HTML, *XML.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Attachment type
:P.Also accepted&colon. *BIN, *TXT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDSMTPEMM/CONTENT'.Content type (CONTENT)
:P.The content type for this command.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PLAIN, *HTML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDSMTPEMM/SMIME'.S/MIME (SMIME)
:P.The s/MIME for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*BOTH:EPK.
:PD.Both.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SIGN, *ENCRYPT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=SNDTCPSPLF.Send TCP/IP Spooled File (SNDTCPSPLF)
:P.Use the Send TCP/IP Spooled File (SNDTCPSPLF) command to send a
spooled file to a remote system's line printer daemon (RFC 1179) through
work/print's LPR client.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDTCPSPLF/RMTSYS'.Remote system (RMTSYS)
:P.The remote system, by host name or internet address.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*INTNETADR:EPK.
:PD.The internet address given in INTNETADR.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 255 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDTCPSPLF/PRTQ'.Printer queue (PRTQ)
:P.The printer queue for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 255 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDTCPSPLF/FILE'.Spooled file (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDTCPSPLF/JOB'.Job name (JOB)
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:PARML.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.User&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Number&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters. The value must be from 000000 to 999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDTCPSPLF/SPLNBR'.Spooled file number (SPLNBR)
:P.The number of the spooled file among the job's spooled files of the
same name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:PT.:PK.*ANY:EPK.
:PD.Any value matches.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDTCPSPLF/JOBSYSNAME'.Job system name (JOBSYSNAME)
:P.The name of the system the job ran on, which tells apart spooled
files that came from other systems.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PK.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PK.*ANY:EPK.
:PD.Any value matches.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDTCPSPLF/CRTDATE'.Spooled file created (CRTDATE)
:P.The date and time the spooled file was created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Creation date
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Creation time
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:PT.:PV.time:EPV.
:PD.Type a time of day&colon. hours, minutes and seconds.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDTCPSPLF/DESTTYP'.Destination type (DESTTYP)
:P.The destination type for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*AS400:EPK.
:PD.This system's native format.
:PT.:PK DEF.*OTHER:EPK.
:PD.Other.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PSF2.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDTCPSPLF/TRANSFORM'.Transform SCS to ASCII (TRANSFORM)
:P.Whether the host print transform converts the SCS data to the
printer's ASCII data stream.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDTCPSPLF/USRDTATFM'.User data transform (USRDTATFM)
:P.The program that transforms the user data of a spooled file before it
is sent to the printer.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDTCPSPLF/MFRTYPMDL'.Manufacturer type and model (MFRTYPMDL)
:P.The manufacturer type and model for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 15 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, *IBM42011 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDTCPSPLF/INTNETADR'.Internet address (INTNETADR)
:P.An internet address in dotted decimal form (IPv4) or in colon form
(IPv6).
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 15 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDTCPSPLF/WSCST'.Workstation customizing object (WSCST)
:P.The workstation customizing object that describes the printer to the
host print transform.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDTCPSPLF/DLTSPLF'.Delete file after sending (DLTSPLF)
:P.Whether to delete file after sending.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDTCPSPLF/DESTOPT'.Destination-dependent options (DESTOPT)
:P.Options passed to the remote system that receives the spooled file.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 128 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDTCPSPLF/SEPPAGE'.Print separator page (SEPPAGE)
:P.Whether a separator page prints before each spooled file.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
